# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps things out of the image.
#
# The name is the convention rather than a choice: BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`
# beside the Dockerfile, and otherwise for `.dockerignore` at the *context* root. A plain
# `.dockerignore` in this directory would be silently ignored — the build would still succeed and
# quietly ship everything below, which is the failure mode worth naming.
#
# The context is the repository root (`docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .`), so every path here is
# relative to the root and not to this directory.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/

# Secrets, and the one class of mistake here with no clean recovery (§14.2, §14.3).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.p8
**/*.p12
**/*.keystore

# Data, not source (§14.3).
backups/
logs/
**/*.pgdump
**/*.binlog

# NOT ignored, deliberately: .git. SourceLink reads the commit out of it at build time and
# /api/v1/about hands it back at runtime, which is an AGPL §13 obligation rather than a nicety
# (§14.6.2). A build without it produces a server that cannot say which commit it is.
